			"Message": "fix(Sky): Fix URI object construction in search results for workbench deduplication\n\nThe previous manual resource object construction (`{ $mid: 1, path, scheme }`) fails when the workbench attempts result deduplication via `uri.with({...})` because it's a POJO without methods. Add `CelUriCtor` and `CelUri` interfaces to type VS Code's URI class, then create `MakeFileUri` that uses the actual `Ctor.file()` method when `__CEL_SERVICES__.URI` is available.\n\nThe lookup is re-resolved on each result construction to handle the event-rescue path where SkyBridge registers before the URI patch binds. Includes a last-resort POJO fallback for edge cases, though the workbench will gracefully fail on dedup in that scenario.\n\nUpdates both `MatchFromHit` (text search results) and file search result mapping to use `MakeFileUri` instead of manual object construction.",
			"SHA": "e9eff04e9a2e6a16986b6817863f204c2c1c3c3e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T09:00:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Refactor worker script loading and improve search provider registration\n\n- Extract worker script imports into dedicated WorkerBundleImports.astro component to fix Astro compiler hoisting issue in JSX conditionals. The previous inline `<script>` inside the ternary was hoisted at parse time, defeating the runtime conditional.\n- Add comprehensive RenderDevLog diagnostics for search operations: textSearch invocation, fileSearch parameters, provider registration, and failure cases.\n- Replace single-shot workbench-ready retry with three parallel rescue paths: event listeners (cel:workbench-ready, cel:services-ready), exponential-ish polling schedule (~10s budget across 10 retries), and manual cel:request-search-register event for late-triggered registration.\n- Add SearchRegistered flag to prevent duplicate registration attempts and ensure proper event listener cleanup.\n\nThis resolves bundle-mode build failures where Astro's script processing couldn't handle conditional rendering, and improves debuggability for search functionality while making registration more resilient to async boot timing.",
			"SHA": "70de1fdb8847585e9298b6999cb443d10b1f7381"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T02:26:36Z",
